  "helpCanvasTitle": "Canvases",
  "helpCanvasBody": "Each canvas keeps its own prompts and generation settings; switch anytime.\n· Only the image count and loop setting are shared across canvases\n💡 Switching canvases doesn't affect generations in progress\n💡 “History” keeps the last 50 generations and can restore them",
  "helpResolutionTitle": "Resolution",
  "helpResolutionBody": "Tiers by total pixels (width × height):\n· Free → up to 1024×1024, inside the green line; needs Opus and ≤28 steps\n· Costs Anlas → beyond the green line; larger sizes cost more\n· Over the limit → beyond 1024×3072 (red line); can't generate",
  "helpImg2imgStrengthTitle": "Strength",
  "helpImg2imgStrengthBody": "How much the original image shapes the result.\n· Lower → closer to the original, fewer changes\n· Higher → more freedom, more repainting\n💡 At 0.01 almost nothing is repainted; with Noise also at minimum → an exact copy of the original\n💡 If the AI ignores your prompt too much, try raising Prompt Guidance",
  "helpImg2imgNoiseTitle": "Noise",
  "helpImg2imgNoiseBody": "Adds extra random noise on top of the original image.\n· 0 → based entirely on the original; more stable results\n· Higher → more creative freedom and new elements\n💡 For originals with large blank areas, raising it lets the AI fill in detail\n💡 Repeated regenerations at high Noise can introduce visual artifacts",
  "helpVibeStrengthTitle": "Reference Strength",
  "helpVibeStrengthBody": "How strongly the Vibe's style affects the image.\n· Higher → closer to the reference's style, colors, and other visual cues\n· Lower → only a light style hint\n💡 With multiple Vibes, keep the total strength ≤ 1\n💡 Too high and the AI starts ignoring the text prompt",
  "helpNormalizeVibeTitle": "Normalize Reference Strength",
  "helpNormalizeVibeBody": "On → all Vibe strengths are scaled down proportionally so the total is ≤ 1\nOff → each Vibe's strength adds up independently",
  "helpInfoExtractedTitle": "Information Extracted",
  "helpInfoExtractedBody": "How much information is extracted from the original image.\n· Lower → high-frequency detail (texture, style) goes first; composition is kept\n· Higher → keeps both composition and texture / style detail\n💡 Setting a new value costs 2 Anlas; previously used values are free\n💡 Can't be changed without the original image",
  "helpCharRefStrengthTitle": "Strength",
  "helpCharRefStrengthBody": "Overall influence of the character / style reference.\n· Higher → reproduces the reference's features more strictly\n· Lower → the reference is only a weak guide\n💡 Each image costs an extra 5 Anlas; multiple references add up\n💡 Too high and facial expression / angle / pose stick too closely to the reference",
  "helpFidelityTitle": "Fidelity",
  "helpFidelityBody": "Whether the prompt can override the reference.\n· Higher → the reference dominates; the prompt can hardly change it\n· Lower → the prompt dominates; easier to adjust the image\n💡 Results vary by image, so experiment",
  "helpStepsTitle": "Steps",
  "helpStepsBody": "Number of sampling steps, i.e. denoising iterations.\nMore steps give finer detail but take longer.\nToo many steps bring diminishing returns or even make things worse.\n💡 28 steps or fewer cost no extra Anlas",
  "helpCfgTitle": "Prompt Guidance (CFG Scale)",
  "helpCfgBody": "How closely the AI follows your prompt.\n· Lower → more freedom; softer, more painterly, dreamy images\n· Higher → follows the description more strictly; finer, sharper detail\n💡 NovelAI recommends 5–6 for V3 and newer models\n💡 Too high backfires: oversaturated colors and broken images",
  "helpVarietyPlusTitle": "Variety+",
  "helpVarietyPlusBody": "Slightly adjusts sampling to vary composition and poses more.\nOn → more variation in composition and poses\nOff → more stable, consistent results\n💡 More noticeable at low Prompt Guidance",
  "helpSamplerTitle": "Sampler",
  "helpSamplerBody": "Determines the denoising path, affecting style and stability.\n· Euler Ancestral — classic all-rounder, high randomness\n· Euler — deterministic version, more stable composition\n· DPM++ 2S Ancestral — rich detail\n· DPM++ 2M SDE — high quality + randomness\n· DPM++ 2M — high-quality deterministic sampling\n· DPM++ SDE — detail and variety combined\n💡 Keep the default, or try DPM++ 2M / Euler Ancestral\n💡 Differences between samplers are more visible at low Steps",
  "helpNoiseScheduleTitle": "Noise Schedule",
  "helpNoiseScheduleBody": "How noise decays at each sampler step, affecting texture.\n· karras — most common; stable with good detail\n· exponential — exponential decay; stronger contrast\n· polyexponential — polynomial decay; smooth transitions\n💡 Keep the default karras",
  "helpSeedTitle": "Seed",
  "helpSeedBody": "The random seed that determines the initial noise.\nSame seed + same settings → nearly identical images\nUseful for locking the composition while fine-tuning.\nEmpty → a different random result each time\n💡 Samplers have slight randomness, so the same seed may still differ a little\n💡 Seeds aren't interchangeable between NAI / Anima / Krea, or with external Stable Diffusion",
  "helpCfgRescaleTitle": "Prompt Guidance Rescale",
  "helpCfgRescaleBody": "Reduces oversaturation and color bleeding from high guidance.\n0 = no correction; higher → stronger correction\nUsually keep 0; with Guidance >7, try 0.1–0.3\n💡 Raise it when edges look over-colored or “deep-fried”",

